  "body": "On Windows, `wire_post` can fail with `Access is denied (os error 5)` (#4159). `post_text()` wrote each call to `camcraft-wire-skims-<process id>.nc`. The tests that call it run in parallel threads of one process, so they shared the path. Windows refuses a write to a file that another thread holds or deletes.\n\nChange: `post_text()` writes into its own `tempfile` directory for each call. The directory is removed when it goes out of scope. The other temp names in this file are used by one test each, so they stay. No production code changes.\n\nReadings:\n- macOS (M5): `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test wire_post`: 28 passed, 0 failed.\n- Windows (`winnie`): see the comment below (run after this PR opened).\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #4159\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
